> The official icon set of the TYPO3 CMS backend: {{ iconCount }} SVG icons for TYPO3 Core, extensions and custom backend modules, published as the npm package `@typo3/icons`, currently version {{ pkg.version }}, under the MIT license.

Every icon is addressed by an identifier such as `actions-document-edit`. The identifier is the whole interface: the Fluid ViewHelper, the web component, the SVG sprite and the Sass variable all resolve the same string, so naming the right icon means naming an identifier from the index at the end of this file.

Icons are monochrome and drawn in `currentColor`, which is why one file serves a light and a dark backend; the only colour of their own is the accent a backend module icon paints a highlight with.

Which TYPO3 release ships which version of the set:

{% for typo3version, version in typo3.versions %}- TYPO3 {{ typo3version }}: `@typo3/icons` {{ version }}
{% endfor %}

An installation shows the icons of the version it ships, not of the newest release. An identifier added after that version does not resolve there.

